{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1776875180,"nonce":"cavxH05Vw/R+FUYflLTMzZ2+AQU=","title":"Retry PROVIDER_OVERLOAD errors with exponential backoff","message":"## Problem\n\nWhen the LLM provider is overloaded (e.g., OpenAI \"high demand\" errors), the Codex CLI does internal retries (1/5 through 5/5) but when those fail, our adapter emits `PROVIDER_OVERLOAD` and stops. We should retry at the adapter level with exponential backoff.\n\nExample error sequence from Codex:\n```\n{\"type\":\"error\",\"message\":\"Reconnecting... 1/5 (We're currently experiencing high demand...)\"}\n...\n{\"type\":\"error\",\"message\":\"Reconnecting... 5/5 (We're currently experiencing high demand...)\"}\n{\"type\":\"turn.failed\",\"error\":{\"message\":\"We're currently experiencing high demand...\"}}\n```\n\n## Solution\n\nExtend `_maybe_retry_transient()` in `HeadlessAgentBase` to also handle `PROVIDER_OVERLOAD` events:\n\n1. Change the type check from `ev.type != AgentEventType.AUTH_FAILURE` to check for both `AUTH_FAILURE` and `PROVIDER_OVERLOAD`\n2. For PROVIDER_OVERLOAD, use longer delays since the provider is under load: [60, 120, 300] seconds\n3. Add a separate retry counter `_overload_retry_count` to track PROVIDER_OVERLOAD retries independently\n\n## Files to modify\n\n- `adapters/agents/base.py`:\n  - Add `OVERLOAD_RETRY_DELAYS = [60, 120, 300]`\n  - Rename `_maybe_retry_transient()` to handle both cases, or add `_maybe_retry_overload()`\n  - Update `stream_events()` to call the retry handler for PROVIDER_OVERLOAD\n\n## Tests\n\n- `test_provider_overload_retries_with_backoff` - PROVIDER_OVERLOAD triggers retry with correct delays\n- `test_provider_overload_max_retries_exceeded` - after 3 retries, event passes through\n- `test_provider_overload_counter_independent` - overload counter separate from transient counter\n\nREQ: REQ-032","files":null}]}